{"book":23,"chapter":20,"context":{"chapter":20,"title":"A Three-Year Living Sign","summary":"When Assyria captures the Philistine city of Ashdod, Isaiah walks stripped and barefoot for three years as a sign that Egypt and Cush, the powers Judah hoped would help, will be led away as captives.","background":"Ashdod rebelled against Assyria and was crushed around 711 BC, a campaign Sargon II's own inscriptions describe. This is the only verse in the Bible that names Sargon; for centuries little else was known of him until his palace was excavated in the 1840s. 'Tartan' is an Assyrian title, the commander-in-chief (compare 2 Kings 18:17).","customs":[{"term":"Naked and barefoot","verses":"20:2-4","note":"Prisoners of war were marched away stripped and barefoot, a deep humiliation. Isaiah, removing his sackcloth and sandals, acts out their fate."}],"watchFor":["The prophet himself becomes the message (v. 3).","'Such is our expectation': trusting Egypt leaves Judah with no escape (v. 6)."],"connections":["2 Kings 18:17","2 Kings 18:21","Micah 1:8","Ezekiel 4:1-3"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["בִּשְׁנַת","bishnat","H8141","HR/Ncfsc","in [the] year"],["בֹּא","bo'","H935","HVqcc","came"],["תַרְתָּן","tartan","H8661","HNcmsa","[the] supreme commander"],["אַשְׁדּוֹדָה","'ashdodah","H795","HNpl/Sd","Ashdod towards"],["בִּשְׁלֹח","bishloch","H7971","HR/Vqcc","when sent"],["אֹתוֹ","'oto","H853","HTo/Sp3ms","<obj.> him"],["סַרְגוֹן","sargon","H5623","HNpm","Sargon"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["אַשּׁוּר","'ashur","H804","HNpl","Assyria"],["וַיִּלָּחֶם","vaiyilachem","H3898","Hc/VNw3ms","and he fought"],["בְּאַשְׁדּוֹד","be'ashdod","H795","HR/Npl","against Ashdod"],["וַיִּלְכְּדָהּ","vaiyilkedah","H3920","Hc/Vqw3ms/Sp3fs","and he captured it"]],"x":[[12018017,12018017,6]],"xn":1},"2":{"w":[["בָּעֵת","ba'et","H6256","HRd/Ncbsa","at the time"],["הַהִיא","hahi'","H1931","HTd/Pp3fs","<the> that"],["דִּבֶּר","diber","H1696","HVpp3ms","he spoke"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","